          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ If a number contains 3 zeros at the end, how many zeros will its square have at the end? "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Six zeros."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.696,
            0.848,
            0.822
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What do you notice about the number of zeros at the end of a number and the number of zeros at the end of its square? Will this always happen? Can we say that squares can only have an even number of zeros at the end? "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Number of zeros at the end of the square is double the number of zeros at the end of a number. Yes. Yes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.828,
            0.847,
            0.895
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ What can you say about the parity of a number and its square? "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Square of an even number is even & square of an odd number is odd."
            }
          ]
        },
